  "data_abstract": "Measurements of antideuteron number fluctuations in Pb-Pb collisions at $\\sqrt{s_\\mathrm{NN}}$ = 5.02 TeV using the ALICE detector at the CERN LHC. Second order cumulant to fitrst order cumulant ratios of antideuteron multiplicity distributions are reported as a function of collision centrality. Furthermore, pearson correlations between measured antideuteron and antiproton are also presented as a function of collision centrality as well as pseudorapidity acceptance.\n",
  "data_keywords": {
